-- title:
--   Characters annihilate Artin symbols of totally positive α≡1 mod conductor
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ and $L$ be number fields with $L$ an extension of $K$ that is Galois over $K$ and whose Galois group $L\simeq_{\mathrm{alg}[K]}L$ is commutative, and let $\psi$ be a group homomorphism from that Galois group to $\mathbb{C}^\times$. Let $\mathfrak m$ be an ideal of $\mathcal O_K$ and let $\alpha\in\mathcal O_K$ be non-zero. Three hypotheses are imposed on $\alpha$: first, the invertible fractional ideal $\mathrm{principalUnit}\,K\,\alpha$ generated by $\alpha$ lies in the subgroup `coprimeToModulus K 𝔪` of the unit group of fractional ideals of $K$, that is, its $v$-adic count vanishes for every height-one prime $v$ of $\mathcal O_K$ whose associated ideal divides $\mathfrak m$; secondly, $\alpha-1$ lies in the ideal [`ArtinL.Abelian.conductor ψ`](def/ArtinL_Abelian.html#L57), the finite product over height-one primes $v$ of $v^{e(v)}$ with exponent $e(v)=(1$ if $\psi$ fails the predicate `IsUnramifiedAt` at $v$, else $0)+\lceil\mathrm{swanConductor}\,\psi\,v\rceil$; thirdly, $\alpha$ is totally positive, i.e. $\tau(\alpha)>0$ for every ring homomorphism $\tau\colon K\to\mathbb R$. The conclusion is that $\psi$ takes the value $1$ on $\mathrm{artinSymbol}\,K\,L\,\mathfrak m$ applied to this element, where `artinSymbol K L 𝔪` is the homomorphism from the primes-coprime-to-$\mathfrak m$ subgroup to the Galois group obtained by sending each height-one prime $v$ to the arithmetic Frobenius `artinFrob K L v` at a prime of $L$ above $v$.
--
--   This is the form of Artin reciprocity used in the project: a character of an abelian extension is trivial on the Artin symbol of any totally positive principal ideal whose generator is congruent to $1$ modulo the conductor of the character. It is invoked by [`ArtinL.Abelian.apply_artinSymbol_eq_prod_sign_of_sub_one_mem_conductor_u0`](thm.html#ArtinL.Abelian.apply_artinSymbol_eq_prod_sign_of_sub_one_mem_conductor_u0), which records the resulting product-of-signs formula, and by [`ArtinL.Abelian.exists_apply_artinSymbol_ne_one_of_conductor_lt_u0`](thm.html#ArtinL.Abelian.exists_apply_artinSymbol_ne_one_of_conductor_lt_u0), which produces a non-trivial value of $\psi$ on an Artin symbol when the conductor is strictly smaller.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ArtinL_Abelian_apply_artinSymbol_eq_one_of_sub_one_mem_conductor_u0.lean

